From d2c73ac0d624347200aa322328c5eb76da055e05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Ravensberg <kevinravensberg@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 20:15:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] quantum-link: coinjoin session messages (AuthorizeCoinjoin,
 GetOwnershipProof)

Adds the two messages a WabiSabi coinjoin remote signer needs beyond the
existing SignPsbt:

- AuthorizeCoinjoinRequest/Response: a one-time session policy (coordinator
  binding, per-round fee cap, round budget, expiry) the user approves on the
  trusted display. Approval returns a session id; sessions are RAM-only on
  the device.
- GetOwnershipProofRequest/Response: a SLIP-0019 ownership proof for one
  input under an authorized session. BIP-322-style signature over the
  coordinator commitment, so SignPsbt cannot express it.

Round signing itself reuses SignPsbt, policy-checked device-side under the
same session. Reference device implementation (policy checks, SLIP-0019
segwit + taproot proofs, session cache) is transport-agnostic and tested:
https://github.com/kravens/KeyOS/tree/feature/passport-coinjoin (os/wallet-rpc-core)

Golden tests included; existing snapshots untouched (enum tags 37-40).
